typedef struct AtomicCounter AtomicCounter;
AtomicCounter* ac_new(void);
void ac_inc(AtomicCounter* ac);
int ac_get(AtomicCounter* ac);
void ac_free(AtomicCounter* ac);

Create a Go binding exposing:

type AtomicCounter struct { c *C.AtomicCounter }
func NewAtomicCounter() (*AtomicCounter, error)
func (a *AtomicCounter) Inc()
func (a *AtomicCounter) Get() int
func (a *AtomicCounter) Close()

In Go, demonstrate safe concurrent usage by launching 3 goroutines, each incrementing the same counter 1000 times, and verify final value is 3000. Include a minimal C header, a stub C implementation that uses a mutex for thread safety, and the Go binding. Show a short Go program that runs in parallel and prints the result?

